            <div xml:id="d780">

                <pb facs="0757" n="657" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg657"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860.00/11: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commissioner at Riga</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Young</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Riga</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-12T23:00:00+01:36"><hi rendition="#italic">August 12,
                                1920—11 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 13—9:27
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>108. Situation slightly better but still very unsatisfactory. British
                    representative here exceedingly pessimistic but I think a little unduly alarmed.
                    The most critical situation is in Esthonia and <pb facs="0758" n="658"
                        xml:id="pg658"/> I have sent Riis there unofficially to assist me in keeping
                    in touch with developments. In Lithuania Bolsheviks thus far carrying out
                    agreement regarding evacuation but the authorities fear trouble when Red army
                    returns from Polish front.</p>
                <p>My preliminary estimate shows 250 American citizens in Baltic Provinces. Will
                    keep you fully informed. Greatly appreciate your prompt action my request for
                    destroyer as on arrival these waters should call at once at Libau, Riga and
                    Reval.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Young</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
